// EXPECTED: compile error
// expect-error: always out of bounds
// Regression (2026-07-28): a range narrowing inside a defer body (which runs at
// scope EXIT) leaked into the intervening code, eliding the fixed-array bounds
// guard (silent OOB). Fixed compiler: idx stays [9,9]. Unfixed: idx proven [2,2].
//
// MOVED to zer_fail 2026-08-17 (BUG-800). `garr[idx]` with idx proven [9,9] on a
// u8[4] is UNCONDITIONALLY and provably out of bounds, which is now a hard error
// instead of an auto-guard that silently returns early. The test still
// discriminates on exactly the property it was written for — and more strongly:
// with the leak, idx is proven [2,2], which is SAFE, so NO error fires and this
// negative FAILS. The error can only appear if the defer-body narrowing did not
// leak.
u8[4] garr;
u32 wild() { return 9; }
u32 main() {
    u32 idx = wild();
    defer { idx = 2; }
    garr[idx] = 7;
    return idx;
}
